{"id":"ef103f0303462b75","group":"58","path":"58/batch07/58-df-transition-density.md","title":"Transition Density","display":"df-transition-density — Transition Density","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-transition-density","aliases":["58-df-transition-density","Transition Density"],"display":"df-transition-density — Transition Density","depends_on":["[[../batch13/58-df-measure.md]]","[[../batch04/58-df-positive-measure.md]]","[[58-df-probability-space.md]]","[[58-df-measurable-function.md]]","[[../batch09/58-df-transition-probability.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-transition-density"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-transition-density</span><span>Transition Density</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-transition-density — Transition Density"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ca832ed6bc22f728\" href=\"?note=ca832ed6bc22f728\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-measure.md\">../batch13/58-df-measure.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"adc7a8154ed79d46\" href=\"?note=adc7a8154ed79d46\" title=\"../batch04/58-df-positive-measure.md\">../batch04/58-df-positive-measure.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"0578a357a86e9d8f\" href=\"?note=0578a357a86e9d8f\" title=\"58-df-probability-space.md\">58-df-probability-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"bbbec05fde1d3b01\" href=\"?note=bbbec05fde1d3b01\" title=\"58-df-measurable-function.md\">58-df-measurable-function.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"5541835907abfd54\" href=\"?note=5541835907abfd54\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-transition-probability.md\">../batch09/58-df-transition-probability.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(E,\\mathcal E)\">\\((E,\\mathcal E)\\)</span> (measurable state space)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"m\">\\(m\\)</span> (reference-measure candidate on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(E,\\mathcal E)\">\\((E,\\mathcal E)\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P:[0,\\infty)\\times E\\times\\mathcal E\\to[0,1]\">\\(P:[0,\\infty)\\times E\\times\\mathcal E\\to[0,1]\\)</span> (transition-probability candidate), with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P_{t,x}(A)=P(t,x,A)\">\\(P_{t,x}(A)=P(t,x,A)\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p:(0,\\infty)\\times E\\times E\\to\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\">\\(p:(0,\\infty)\\times E\\times E\\to\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\)</span> (density candidate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p_{t,x}:E\\to\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\">\\(p_{t,x}:E\\to\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\)</span> denotes <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"y\\mapsto p(t,x,y)\">\\(y\\mapsto p(t,x,y)\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{TransitionProbability}_S(P,E,\\mathcal E)\">\\(\\mathrm{TransitionProbability}_S(P,E,\\mathcal E)\\)</span> (transition-probability predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"5541835907abfd54\" href=\"?note=5541835907abfd54\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-transition-probability.md\">../batch09/58-df-transition-probability.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SigmaFinite}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{SigmaFinite}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Measurable}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Measurable}_S\\)</span> (source predicates)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{TransitionDensity}_S(p,P,m;E,\\mathcal E)\">\\(\\operatorname{TransitionDensity}_S(p,P,m;E,\\mathcal E)\\)</span> (transition-density predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}transition\\text{-}density} \\vdash \\operatorname{TransitionDensity}_S(p,P,m;E,\\mathcal E)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{TransitionProbability}_S(P,E,\\mathcal E)\\land\\mathrm{SigmaFinite}_S(m,E,\\mathcal E)\\land p\\in(\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})^{\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\times E\\times E}\\land\\forall t\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall x\\in E\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(p_{t,x};(E,\\mathcal E),(\\mathbb R_{\\geq0},\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})))\\land\\forall A\\in\\mathcal E\\;\\bigl(P(t,x,A)=\\int_A p(t,x,y)\\,m(dy)\\bigr)\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}transition\\text{-}density} \\vdash \\operatorname{TransitionDensity}_S(p,P,m;E,\\mathcal E)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{TransitionProbability}_S(P,E,\\mathcal E)\\land\\mathrm{SigmaFinite}_S(m,E,\\mathcal E)\\land p\\in(\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})^{\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\times E\\times E}\\land\\forall t\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall x\\in E\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(p_{t,x};(E,\\mathcal E),(\\mathbb R_{\\geq0},\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})))\\land\\forall A\\in\\mathcal E\\;\\bigl(P(t,x,A)=\\int_A p(t,x,y)\\,m(dy)\\bigr)\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Transition density: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p_t(x, y)\">\\(p_t(x, y)\\)</span> such that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P_t(x, \\cdot) = p_t(x, \\cdot) m\">\\(P_t(x, \\cdot) = p_t(x, \\cdot) m\\)</span></li>\n<li>The imported transition-probability predicate supplies the kernel measurability, probability normalization, and Chapman--Kolmogorov law that were previously only assumed in prose.</li>\n<li>Existence of a transition density requires <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P_t(x,\\cdot)\\ll m\">\\(P_t(x,\\cdot)\\ll m\\)</span>; the Feller property alone does not guarantee such absolute continuity.</li>\n<li>Normalization follows from <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P_t(x,E)=1\">\\(P_t(x,E)=1\\)</span>. Chapman--Kolmogorov yields the convolution identity for suitable versions, generally <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"m\">\\(m\\)</span>-almost everywhere in the terminal variable.</li>\n<li>Heat kernel: Gaussian kernel for Brownian motion; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p_t(x, y) = (2\\pi t)^{-n/2} e^{-|x-y|^2/(2t)}\">\\(p_t(x, y) = (2\\pi t)^{-n/2} e^{-|x-y|^2/(2t)}\\)</span></li>\n<li>Spectral representation: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p_t(x, y) = \\sum_n e^{-\\lambda_n t} \\phi_n(x) \\phi_n(y)\">\\(p_t(x, y) = \\sum_n e^{-\\lambda_n t} \\phi_n(x) \\phi_n(y)\\)</span></li>\n<li>Short-time asymptotics: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p_t(x, y) \\sim (4\\pi t)^{-n/2} e^{-d(x,y)^2/(4t)}\">\\(p_t(x, y) \\sim (4\\pi t)^{-n/2} e^{-d(x,y)^2/(4t)}\\)</span> (Varadhan)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Rogers and Williams, Diffusions, Markov Processes and Martingales</li>\n<li>Bass, Probabilistic Techniques in Analysis</li>\n<li>Chung, Lectures from Markov Processes to Brownian Motion</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch13/58-df-measure.md","status":"resolved","id":"ca832ed6bc22f728","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-measure.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch04/58-df-positive-measure.md","status":"resolved","id":"adc7a8154ed79d46","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch04/58-df-positive-measure.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-probability-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"0578a357a86e9d8f","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-probability-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-measurable-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"bbbec05fde1d3b01","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-measurable-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch09/58-df-transition-probability.md","status":"resolved","id":"5541835907abfd54","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-transition-probability.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch09/58-df-transition-probability.md","status":"resolved","id":"5541835907abfd54","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{TransitionProbability}_S(P,E,\\mathcal E)$ (transition-probability predicate, see [[../batch09/58-df-transition-probability.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"(E,\\mathcal E)","display":false},{"tex":"m","display":false},{"tex":"(E,\\mathcal E)","display":false},{"tex":"P:[0,\\infty)\\times E\\times\\mathcal E\\to[0,1]","display":false},{"tex":"P_{t,x}(A)=P(t,x,A)","display":false},{"tex":"p:(0,\\infty)\\times E\\times E\\to\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}","display":false},{"tex":"p_{t,x}:E\\to\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}","display":false},{"tex":"y\\mapsto p(t,x,y)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{TransitionProbability}_S(P,E,\\mathcal E)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SigmaFinite}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ProbabilityMeasure}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Measurable}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{TransitionDensity}_S(p,P,m;E,\\mathcal E)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}transition\\text{-}density} \\vdash \\operatorname{TransitionDensity}_S(p,P,m;E,\\mathcal E)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{TransitionProbability}_S(P,E,\\mathcal E)\\land\\mathrm{SigmaFinite}_S(m,E,\\mathcal E)\\land p\\in(\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})^{\\mathbb R_{>0}\\times E\\times E}\\land\\forall t\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\\forall x\\in E\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(p_{t,x};(E,\\mathcal E),(\\mathbb R_{\\geq0},\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})))\\land\\forall A\\in\\mathcal E\\;\\bigl(P(t,x,A)=\\int_A p(t,x,y)\\,m(dy)\\bigr)\\Bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"p_t(x, y)","display":false},{"tex":"P_t(x, \\cdot) = p_t(x, \\cdot) m","display":false},{"tex":"P_t(x,\\cdot)\\ll m","display":false},{"tex":"P_t(x,E)=1","display":false},{"tex":"m","display":false},{"tex":"p_t(x, y) = (2\\pi t)^{-n/2} e^{-|x-y|^2/(2t)}","display":false},{"tex":"p_t(x, y) = \\sum_n e^{-\\lambda_n t} \\phi_n(x) \\phi_n(y)","display":false},{"tex":"p_t(x, y) \\sim (4\\pi t)^{-n/2} e^{-d(x,y)^2/(4t)}","display":false}],"bytes":2777,"backlinks":[{"id":"c26859179739aef8","anchor":"ref-2","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1313","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-df-transition-density.md|58-df-transition-density]]（batch07）"}],"outgoing":["ca832ed6bc22f728","adc7a8154ed79d46","0578a357a86e9d8f","bbbec05fde1d3b01","5541835907abfd54"]}